//@version=5
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  PO3 Levels & Kihon Suchi  —  a Pine v5 port of PO3_Levels.mq5
//
//  Same instrument, same arithmetic, on TradingView instead of MetaTrader:
//
//    · Power of Three levels around price, one checkbox and one colour per
//      PO3 number from 3 to 19683, merged so the highest number owns a level
//    · Candles counted from the year, month, week and day opens, with the
//      Ichimoku kihon suchi numbers marked on that count
//    · The count panel, the nested M1 count, and the segment block that
//      counts the minutes inside a kihon H4 or H1 candle
//    · Countdown on the developing candle, and the session screen-time clock
//
//  Pine has no #include, so the two MQL headers are inlined below rather than
//  referenced: PO3_Kihon.mqh becomes the "Kihon suchi" section and
//  PO3_Core.mqh the "PO3 level maths" section, both kept whole and kept first,
//  so the port can be read against the originals function by function.
//
//  WHAT THE PLATFORM CHANGES. Everything here is a Pine limit, not a decision:
//
//    · Drawing budget. Pine allows 500 lines and 500 labels per script, where
//      MT5 has no practical ceiling. "Levels each side of price" is therefore
//      clamped to 25 rather than 100, which caps nine ticked grids at 450
//      lines. Level labels have their own budget, and the panel says so when
//      it bites rather than dropping them quietly.
//    · No z-order. Pine drawings are always in front of the candles, so
//      "Draw lines behind the candles" has no equivalent and is not offered.
//      The kihon vertical lines are drawn dotted and dimmed instead.
//    · The panel is a table. Tables are pinned to one of nine positions, not
//      to a pixel offset, so Corner and "Centre it vertically" survive but the
//      X and Y distances do not. The two blocks share one table, side by side,
//      which is what "beside, sharing a top edge" comes to here.
//    · Text sizes are buckets. Pine takes tiny/small/normal/large/huge, not a
//      point size, so the size inputs offer those instead of 5-24.
//    · No timer. MT5 redraws the countdown once a second off OnTimer; Pine
//      only runs on a tick or a bar update, so a quiet market leaves the
//      countdown showing the last tick's figure rather than counting down
//      through the silence.
//    · No terminal globals. The session clock therefore restarts whenever the
//      script reloads, which on TradingView includes a timeframe change - the
//      one thing the MT5 version goes out of its way to survive.
//    · Server time is read as the exchange timezone, which is the nearest
//      thing TradingView has to a broker's clock.
//
//  Counting is inclusive at both ends, as it is in the MQL: the candle sitting
//  at the anchor is candle 1, not candle 0. That single convention is the
//  whole of the kihon arithmetic.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

indicator("PO3 Levels & Kihon Suchi", "PO3 + Kihon", overlay = true,
     max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 10,
     max_bars_back = 2000)


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  Kihon suchi — Ichimoku's basic time numbers.        (was PO3_Kihon.mqh)
//
//  The count is inclusive at both ends: the candle you start from is candle 1,
//  not candle 0. Two 17-spans laid end to end do not make 34, because the last
//  candle of the first span IS the first candle of the second: 17 + 17 - 1 =
//  33. Every compound number is built that way, by chaining simple spans that
//  share their turning candle.
//
//  THE SIMPLE NUMBERS (tanjun kihon suchi) - 9, 17, 26
//      9   ichi-moku, the span the Tenkan is built on
//      17  9 + 9 - 1
//      26  GIVEN, not derived. The Kijun span and the cloud displacement, and
//          historically a month of trading days under the six-day week Japan
//          kept when this was written. It is the one number the overlap rule
//          does not produce - see the note below.
//
//  THE COMPOUND NUMBERS (fukugo kihon suchi)
//      33   17 + 17 - 1          76   26 + 26 + 26 - 2  (also 51 + 26 - 1)
//      42   26 + 17 - 1          129  65 + 65 - 1
//      51   26 + 26 - 1          172  65 + 42 + 42 + 26 - 3
//      65   33 + 33 - 1          226  76 + 76 + 76 - 2
//           (four 17s chained)   257  129 + 129 - 1
//
//  26 is the exception, not 172. Every compound above chains simple spans
//  sharing a candle, so k spans subtract k-1. 26 does not come out that way:
//  three 9s chained give 9+9+9-2 = 25, and 17+9-1 is 25 as well. Reaching 26
//  needs either a plain 9+17 with no shared candle or 9+9+9-1 with one overlap
//  too few, and neither is the rule. That is expected - 26 is one of the three
//  SIMPLE numbers, and a simple number is a given, not a result. It is a
//  calendar figure that the rule then builds on.
//
//  Above 257 the series keeps doubling - 257 + 257 - 1 = 513 - but a number
//  that large has no meaning on an intraday chart, where even 257 M1 candles
//  is only a little over four hours. The list stops where the classical one
//  stops.
//
//  What the numbers are FOR: they are candidate turning points in TIME, not in
//  price. They say nothing about direction. Read them against the PO3 grid
//  below: a kihon suchi candle landing on a 27 or 81 level is time and price
//  agreeing, which is the only reason both halves are in one script.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// 3 simple + 9 compound. The simple ones come first and the whole list is
// ascending, so a scan can stop early and the first KIHON_SIMPLE entries are
// exactly the simple numbers.
KIHON_SIMPLE = 3
KIHON_COUNT  = 12
var KIHON = array.from(9, 17, 26, 33, 42, 51, 65, 76, 129, 172, 226, 257)

// Ceiling on how many candles a count will chase. Past 257 every count reads
// the same - there is no kihon number above it - so an exact figure buys
// nothing. Beyond this the count reports "too far" instead. Deliberately far
// above 257 so a legitimate deep count, a week of M1 at around 7200, is still
// counted exactly.
KIHON_SPAN_CAP = 20000

// Is n a kihon suchi number. The compound flag is a filter, not a separate
// list: pass false and only 9, 17 and 26 answer true, which is the quiet chart.
kihonIs(n, withCompound) =>
    last = withCompound ? KIHON_COUNT : KIHON_SIMPLE
    hit = false
    for i = 0 to last - 1
        k = array.get(KIHON, i)
        if k == n
            hit := true
            break
        if k > n                              // ascending, so no point going on
            break
    hit

// The next kihon suchi number strictly above n, or 0 past the end. Strictly
// above, so standing ON 26 tells you 33 is next rather than repeating the
// number you are already on.
kihonNext(n, withCompound) =>
    last = withCompound ? KIHON_COUNT : KIHON_SIMPLE
    nx = 0
    for i = 0 to last - 1
        k = array.get(KIHON, i)
        if k > n
            nx := k
            break
    nx

// The last kihon suchi number at or below n, or 0 below the first.
kihonAtOrBelow(n, withCompound) =>
    last = withCompound ? KIHON_COUNT : KIHON_SIMPLE
    best = 0
    for i = 0 to last - 1
        k = array.get(KIHON, i)
        if k <= n
            best := k
        else
            break
    best

// Signed distance from n to the NEAREST kihon suchi number.
//
// 0 means n is one. Negative means the number is still ahead: 7 returns -2,
// two candles short of 9. Positive means it has just gone by: 11 returns +2.
//
// The sign convention is n minus the number, so it reads the way the chart
// does - a count running up towards a level shows a negative gap closing to
// zero, then goes positive as it leaves.
//
// Nearest, not next, because either side matters. A count two candles PAST 26
// is as much "around 26" as one two candles short of it, and a turn that was
// due at 26 is not cancelled by the candle after it.
kihonOffset(n, withCompound) =>
    last = withCompound ? KIHON_COUNT : KIHON_SIMPLE
    best = n - array.get(KIHON, 0)
    for i = 1 to last - 1
        d = n - array.get(KIHON, i)
        if math.abs(d) < math.abs(best)
            best := d
    best

// The last number of the ACTIVE list: with the compounds switched off the
// series ends at 26, not at 257.
kihonLast(withCompound) =>
    array.get(KIHON, (withCompound ? KIHON_COUNT : KIHON_SIMPLE) - 1)


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  PO3 level maths.                                     (was PO3_Core.mqh)
//
//  A level is  multiplier x 3^n / scale.  At scale 1 every level is a whole
//  number, so the gold grid lands on 4374, 4383, 4392 and so on. Powers of
//  three nest, so every 27 level is also a 9 level: the 27 grid is the
//  every-third member of the 9 grid. That nesting is what gives a 27 range its
//  three 9 cells, and the equilibrium of that range is its midpoint.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// The epsilon is not cosmetic. A price sitting exactly on a level, 2952.45
// against PO3 2187, divides to 134.99999999999997 rather than 135, so a bare
// floor() would anchor one level too low and shift the whole window down.
PO3_EPS = 1e-9

// Multiplier index of the level at or below price.
po3Index(price, po3, scale) =>
    int(math.floor(price * scale / po3 + PO3_EPS))

// Price of the level with this multiplier. The multiply is done in integers
// and divided once, so the result is the nearest float to the exact figure.
// m * (po3/scale) would accumulate drift across the grid.
po3Level(m, po3, scale) =>
    (m * po3) / scale

// Spacing between adjacent levels of this grid.
po3Step(po3, scale) =>
    po3 / scale

// The level at or below price.
po3Floor(price, po3, scale) =>
    po3Level(po3Index(price, po3, scale), po3, scale)


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  The counts themselves — KihonAnchor, KihonCount and KihonSegmentStart,
//  rewritten for Pine's execution model.
//
//  MT5 asks "how many bars of timeframe T lie between the anchor and now" and
//  the terminal answers from its own history. Pine has no such call, so each
//  count is computed IN THE CONTEXT OF THE TIMEFRAME BEING COUNTED, by
//  counting bars since the anchor condition was last true, and pulled back
//  into the chart's context with request.security. ta.barssince returns 0 on
//  the bar the condition fired, so +1 gives the inclusive count MT5 produces
//  and the anchor candle is candle 1.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// Where the candle count starts. Same order as ENUM_KIHON_ANCHOR in the MQL,
// so the numbers below are that enum.
ANCHOR_DAY   = 0
ANCHOR_WEEK  = 1
ANCHOR_MONTH = 2
ANCHOR_YEAR  = 3
ANCHOR_TIME  = 4

// True on the first candle of the anchor's period, in the current context.
//
// Day and week come from the D1 and W1 boundaries themselves, so they follow
// the exchange's own session rollover rather than a guess at it - the same
// reason the MQL reads iTime(PERIOD_D1) instead of computing midnight. Month
// and year are calendar boundaries, so a weekly candle straddling New Year
// belongs to the old year.
//
// A custom time is a session open, CLAMPED to the day open. The clamp is the
// part worth explaining: without it, an 08:00 anchor read at 03:00 on Monday
// would roll back to 08:00 on FRIDAY and count the whole weekend gap. Clamped,
// a session anchor never counts across a day boundary - before the session
// opens you get the count from the day open, and the moment it opens the count
// restarts from there.
kihonAnchorHere(mode, hh, mm) =>
    newD = timeframe.change("D")
    newW = timeframe.change("W")
    newM = timeframe.change("M")
    newY = timeframe.change("12M")

    tod = hour(time, syminfo.timezone) * 60 + minute(time, syminfo.timezone)
    tgt = math.min(23, math.max(0, hh)) * 60 + math.min(59, math.max(0, mm))

    crossed = tod >= tgt
    var wasCrossed = false
    // newD carries the clamp: until the session time arrives the day open is
    // the anchor, and the first bar at or past it takes over.
    sess = newD or (crossed and not wasCrossed)
    wasCrossed := crossed

    mode == ANCHOR_WEEK ? newW : mode == ANCHOR_MONTH ? newM :
      mode == ANCHOR_YEAR ? newY : mode == ANCHOR_TIME ? sess : newD

// Candles since that anchor, inclusive, in the current context. 0 means the
// answer is not known yet - history still loading, or the anchor older than
// the bars this chart holds - so a caller can tell "nothing to show" from
// "candle zero", which does not exist under inclusive counting.
kihonCountHere(mode, hh, mm) =>
    n = ta.barssince(kihonAnchorHere(mode, hh, mm))
    na(n) ? 0 : n + 1

// Candles since the open of the containing candle of a COARSER timeframe -
// the segment block's count, which starts at a candle rather than a calendar
// period. Everything it measures is inside that one candle.
kihonSinceHere(coarse) =>
    n = ta.barssince(timeframe.change(coarse))
    na(n) ? 0 : n + 1

// The nested M1 count, and the hour it restarted at.       (KihonSegmentStart)
//
// Run across a whole day an M1 count is past 257 by breakfast and says nothing
// for the rest of the session, so it restarts at every kihon suchi H1 candle
// instead: at H1 candle 1, again at 9, again at 17. A day is not long enough
// to reach 26.
//
// The reset lands ON the kihon candle, not after it - as the ninth hour opens
// the M1 count reads 1. segNo carries the hour it restarted at, because the
// count alone cannot tell you which phase of the day it is measuring.
//
// h is the H1 candle number since the day open, tracked on the M1 series
// because that is the series this runs on. Until the first day boundary in the
// loaded history there is no h to count from, so the count reports 0 rather
// than a number counted from an unknown start.
kihonNestedM1(mode, hh, mm, withCompound) =>
    dayCond = kihonAnchorHere(mode, hh, mm)
    newH1   = timeframe.change("60")

    var h   = 0
    var seg = 0
    var c   = 0

    if dayCond
        h   := 1
        seg := 1
        c   := 1
    else if newH1
        h := h + 1
        if kihonIs(h, withCompound)
            seg := h
            c   := 1
        else
            c := c + 1
    else
        c := c + 1

    [h > 0 ? c : 0, seg]


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  Inputs
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

gGrid = "Grid"
InpScale    = input.float(1.0, "Scale divisor (1 = whole numbers, 100 = workbook 2dp)",
     minval = 0.000001, group = gGrid)
// Pine allows 500 lines per script where MT5 has no practical ceiling, so the
// MQL's 1..100 becomes 1..25: nine ticked grids at 25 each side is 450 lines,
// which fits with room left for the kihon marks.
InpEachSide = input.int(3, "Levels each side of price", minval = 1, maxval = 25,
     group = gGrid, tooltip = "Applies per ticked grid. Capped at 25 by Pine's " +
     "500-line budget, where the MetaTrader build allows 100.")

gLbl = "Labels"
InpShowLabels  = input.bool(true, "Write the PO3 number on each line", group = gLbl)
InpLabelMinPO3 = input.int(3, "Label only levels of PO3 >=", minval = 3, maxval = 19683,
     group = gLbl, tooltip = "Every label shares one time anchor, so raise this " +
     "if the fine grids stack digits.")
InpFontSize    = input.string(size.tiny, "Label text size", group = gLbl,
     options = [size.tiny, size.small, size.normal, size.large, size.huge])
InpLabelShift  = input.int(10, "Label gap right of the last candle, in bars",
     minval = -50, maxval = 400, group = gLbl,
     tooltip = "Positive tabs the numbers off the candles into the empty space " +
     "at the right, level with their own lines and beside the price scale. " +
     "Raise it to sit closer to the scale - how much room there is comes from " +
     "the chart's own right margin, which Pine cannot read. 0 or less ends the " +
     "text at the anchor instead, over the candles, which is the MetaTrader " +
     "build's default.")

gClk = "Candle countdown"
InpShowClock   = input.bool(true, "Show time left on the current candle", group = gClk,
     tooltip = "Pine has no one-second timer, so this refreshes on a tick rather " +
     "than counting down through a quiet market.")
InpClockShift  = input.int(1, "Bars right of the developing candle", minval = -10,
     maxval = 400, group = gClk)
InpClockGapPts = input.int(0, "Vertical offset from price, in ticks (+ up)", group = gClk)
InpClockSize   = input.string(size.small, "Text size", group = gClk,
     options = [size.tiny, size.small, size.normal, size.large, size.huge])
InpClockColor  = input.color(#00FF00, "Text colour", group = gClk)

gSes = "Session timer"
InpShowSession  = input.bool(true, "Show time spent on this chart", group = gSes,
     tooltip = "Wall-clock time since the script loaded. Pine has no terminal " +
     "globals, so unlike the MetaTrader build this DOES restart on a timeframe change.")
InpSessionPos   = input.string("Top right", "Corner", group = gSes,
     options = ["Top left", "Top right", "Bottom left", "Bottom right"])
InpSessionSize  = input.string(size.normal, "Text size", group = gSes,
     options = [size.tiny, size.small, size.normal, size.large, size.huge])
InpSessionColor = input.color(#C0C0C0, "Text colour", group = gSes)
InpSessionLimit = input.int(0, "Minutes on chart before it turns red (0 = off)",
     minval = 0, group = gSes)
InpSessionOver  = input.color(#FF6347, "Text colour once over the limit", group = gSes)

gCnt = "Candle count"
InpShowCount   = input.bool(true, "Draw the count on the chart", group = gCnt)
InpCountAnchor = input.string("Day open", "Count from", group = gCnt,
     options = ["Day open", "Week open", "Month open", "Year open", "Custom time of day"])
InpAnchorHour  = input.int(8, "Custom anchor, hour (exchange time)", minval = 0,
     maxval = 23, group = gCnt)
InpAnchorMin   = input.int(0, "Custom anchor, minute", minval = 0, maxval = 59, group = gCnt)
InpMarkOpen    = input.bool(true, "Line on the candle the count starts at", group = gCnt)
InpOpenColor   = input.color(#696969, "Open line colour", group = gCnt)

gKih = "Kihon suchi"
InpMarkKihon     = input.bool(true, "Mark the kihon suchi candles", group = gKih)
InpKihonCompound = input.bool(true, "Include the compound numbers (33 and up)", group = gKih)
InpKihonLines    = input.bool(true, "Vertical line on each marked candle", group = gKih)
InpKihonSimple   = input.color(#00BFFF, "9, 17, 26 — colour", group = gKih)
InpKihonComp     = input.color(#BA55D3, "33 and up — colour", group = gKih)
InpKihonSize     = input.string(size.small, "Marker text size", group = gKih,
     options = [size.tiny, size.small, size.normal, size.large, size.huge])
InpKihonGapPts   = input.int(0, "Marker offset from the candle low, in ticks", group = gKih)
InpNumberAll     = input.bool(false, "Number every candle, not just the kihon ones",
     group = gKih, tooltip = "Capped at the most recent 300 candles.")

gPnl = "Candle count panel"
InpShowPanel    = input.bool(true, "Show the count panel", group = gPnl)
InpShowYear     = input.bool(true, "Year block — MN1, W1, D1", group = gPnl)
InpShowMonth    = input.bool(true, "Month block — D1, H4, H1", group = gPnl)
InpShowWeek     = input.bool(true, "Week block — H4, H1, M30", group = gPnl)
InpShowDay      = input.bool(true, "Day block — H1 to chart", group = gPnl)
InpPanelCorner  = input.string("Left upper", "Corner", group = gPnl,
     options = ["Left upper", "Left lower", "Right upper", "Right lower"])
InpPanelMiddle  = input.bool(true, "Centre it vertically", group = gPnl)
InpPanelSize    = input.string(size.small, "Text size (panel)", group = gPnl,
     options = [size.tiny, size.small, size.normal, size.large, size.huge])
InpPanelBox     = input.bool(true, "Solid block behind the panel", group = gPnl)
InpPanelBg      = input.color(#121218, "Block colour", group = gPnl)
InpPanelBorder  = input.color(#696969, "Block border colour", group = gPnl)
InpPanelColor   = input.color(#C0C0C0, "Text colour (panel)", group = gPnl)
InpPanelHit     = input.color(#00FF00, "Colour of a row standing ON a kihon number",
     group = gPnl)
InpPanelNear    = input.color(#FFA500, "Colour of a row within reach of one", group = gPnl)
InpPanelNearTol = input.int(2, "How many candles either side counts as near",
     minval = 0, maxval = 8, group = gPnl, tooltip = "0 switches the orange state off.")

gSeg = "Kihon segment panel"
InpShowSeg = input.bool(true, "Show the kihon segment panel", group = gSeg,
     tooltip = "The block beside the count panel: M15, M5 and M1 inside a kihon " +
     "H4 or H1 candle.")
InpSegH4   = input.bool(true, "Segments inside a kihon H4 candle", group = gSeg)
InpSegH1   = input.bool(true, "Segments inside a kihon H1 candle", group = gSeg)

// Every grid is on by default: the model is the whole nest of powers, and a
// level's strength is meant to be read from how many grids agree on it, which
// is only visible with all of them drawn. Untick the fine ones for a quieter
// chart; the levels that remain do not move.
gPO3 = "PO3 levels to show"
InpUse_3     = input.bool(true,  "3 — show",     group = gPO3, inline = "p3")
InpCol_3     = input.color(#808080, "",          group = gPO3, inline = "p3")
InpUse_9     = input.bool(true,  "9 — show",     group = gPO3, inline = "p9")
InpCol_9     = input.color(#A9A9A9, "",          group = gPO3, inline = "p9")
InpUse_27    = input.bool(true,  "27 — show",    group = gPO3, inline = "p27")
InpCol_27    = input.color(#5F9EA0, "",          group = gPO3, inline = "p27")
InpUse_81    = input.bool(true,  "81 — show",    group = gPO3, inline = "p81")
InpCol_81    = input.color(#4682B4, "",          group = gPO3, inline = "p81")
InpUse_243   = input.bool(true,  "243 — show",   group = gPO3, inline = "p243")
InpCol_243   = input.color(#3CB371, "",          group = gPO3, inline = "p243")
InpUse_729   = input.bool(true,  "729 — show",   group = gPO3, inline = "p729")
InpCol_729   = input.color(#FF8C00, "",          group = gPO3, inline = "p729")
InpUse_2187  = input.bool(true,  "2187 — show",  group = gPO3, inline = "p2187")
InpCol_2187  = input.color(#DAA520, "",          group = gPO3, inline = "p2187")
InpUse_6561  = input.bool(true,  "6561 — show",  group = gPO3, inline = "p6561")
InpCol_6561  = input.color(#FF4500, "",          group = gPO3, inline = "p6561")
InpUse_19683 = input.bool(true,  "19683 — show", group = gPO3, inline = "p19683")
InpCol_19683 = input.color(#DC143C, "",          group = gPO3, inline = "p19683")

// The anchor mode, as the enum number the counting functions take.
anchorMode = InpCountAnchor == "Week open" ? ANCHOR_WEEK :
     InpCountAnchor == "Month open" ? ANCHOR_MONTH :
     InpCountAnchor == "Year open" ? ANCHOR_YEAR :
     InpCountAnchor == "Custom time of day" ? ANCHOR_TIME : ANCHOR_DAY

// The open the day block counts from. The chart's own anchor when that anchor
// is a custom session time, so the panel agrees with the marks drawn on the
// chart instead of quietly counting from a different open; the plain day open
// otherwise, since every other anchor mode belongs to one of the blocks above
// the day block.
daySess = anchorMode == ANCHOR_TIME
dayMode = daySess ? ANCHOR_TIME : ANCHOR_DAY


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  The counts, pulled back from each timeframe's own context.
//
//  Every request.security call lives here, at global scope and unconditional,
//  because Pine will not have them inside an if or a loop. A row that is
//  switched off is therefore still counted and simply not shown, which costs a
//  request and keeps the call graph legal.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

LK = barmerge.lookahead_off

// Year block — months, weeks and trading days since 1 January
cMN1_Y = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "M", kihonCountHere(ANCHOR_YEAR, 0, 0), lookahead = LK)
cW1_Y  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "W", kihonCountHere(ANCHOR_YEAR, 0, 0), lookahead = LK)
cD1_Y  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", kihonCountHere(ANCHOR_YEAR, 0, 0), lookahead = LK)

// Month block — since the 1st
cD1_M = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D",   kihonCountHere(ANCHOR_MONTH, 0, 0), lookahead = LK)
cH4_M = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "240", kihonCountHere(ANCHOR_MONTH, 0, 0), lookahead = LK)
cH1_M = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "60",  kihonCountHere(ANCHOR_MONTH, 0, 0), lookahead = LK)

// Week block — since the week open
cH4_W  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "240", kihonCountHere(ANCHOR_WEEK, 0, 0), lookahead = LK)
cH1_W  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "60",  kihonCountHere(ANCHOR_WEEK, 0, 0), lookahead = LK)
cM30_W = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "30",  kihonCountHere(ANCHOR_WEEK, 0, 0), lookahead = LK)

// Day block — H1 down to the chart's own period
cH1_D  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "60", kihonCountHere(dayMode, InpAnchorHour, InpAnchorMin), lookahead = LK)
cM30_D = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "30", kihonCountHere(dayMode, InpAnchorHour, InpAnchorMin), lookahead = LK)
cM15_D = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "15", kihonCountHere(dayMode, InpAnchorHour, InpAnchorMin), lookahead = LK)
cM5_D  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "5",  kihonCountHere(dayMode, InpAnchorHour, InpAnchorMin), lookahead = LK)

// The nested M1 count, and the hour it restarted at
[cM1_N, segNo] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "1",
     kihonNestedM1(dayMode, InpAnchorHour, InpAnchorMin, InpKihonCompound), lookahead = LK)

// Inside a kihon H4, and inside a kihon H1
sM15_H4 = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "15", kihonSinceHere("240"), lookahead = LK)
sM5_H4  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "5",  kihonSinceHere("240"), lookahead = LK)
sM1_H4  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "1",  kihonSinceHere("240"), lookahead = LK)
sM5_H1  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "5",  kihonSinceHere("60"),  lookahead = LK)
sM1_H1  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "1",  kihonSinceHere("60"),  lookahead = LK)

// The count on the CHART's own timeframe, for the marks. No request needed -
// this is the context the script already runs in.
cChart = InpShowCount ? kihonCountHere(anchorMode, InpAnchorHour, InpAnchorMin) : 0

// Block anchors, for the titles and the span-cap check.
yearOpen  = timestamp(syminfo.timezone, year(timenow, syminfo.timezone), 1, 1, 0, 0)
monthOpen = timestamp(syminfo.timezone, year(timenow, syminfo.timezone),
     month(timenow, syminfo.timezone), 1, 0, 0)
weekOpen = time("W")
dayOpen  = time("D")
h4Open   = time("240")
h1Open   = time("60")

// Period lengths, resolved once. The panel compares by LENGTH rather than by
// position in a list, so a non-standard chart period lands where its length
// puts it instead of falling through.
SEC_M1  = timeframe.in_seconds("1")
SEC_M5  = timeframe.in_seconds("5")
SEC_M15 = timeframe.in_seconds("15")
SEC_M30 = timeframe.in_seconds("30")
SEC_H1  = timeframe.in_seconds("60")
SEC_H4  = timeframe.in_seconds("240")
SEC_D1  = timeframe.in_seconds("D")
SEC_W1  = timeframe.in_seconds("W")
SEC_MN1 = timeframe.in_seconds("M")
chartSecs = timeframe.in_seconds()

// MetaTrader's own name for the chart's period, so the countdown reads the way
// the MQL's does.
chartTf = chartSecs < 60 ? "S" + str.tostring(chartSecs) :
     chartSecs < 3600 ? "M" + str.tostring(chartSecs / 60) :
     chartSecs < 86400 ? "H" + str.tostring(chartSecs / 3600) :
     chartSecs == 86400 ? "D1" : chartSecs < 2592000 ? "W1" : "MN1"


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  Formatting
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

pad2(n) =>
    (n < 10 ? "0" : "") + str.tostring(n)

// A span of seconds in units that suit its size: mm:ss under an hour, hh:mm:ss
// above it, and days once past one. The candle countdown and the session timer
// both format through here, so M15 reads 14:59 while an hour on the chart
// reads 01:00:00.
hms(secs) =>
    s0 = math.max(0, secs)
    d  = int(s0 / 86400)
    s1 = s0 - d * 86400
    h  = int(s1 / 3600)
    s2 = s1 - h * 3600
    m  = int(s2 / 60)
    s3 = s2 - m * 60
    d > 0 ? str.tostring(d) + "d " + pad2(h) + ":" + pad2(m) + ":" + pad2(s3) :
      h > 0 ? pad2(h) + ":" + pad2(m) + ":" + pad2(s3) : pad2(m) + ":" + pad2(s3)

// Whole levels print without decimals, so a scale 1 gold level reads 4374
// rather than 4374.00.
priceText(p) =>
    math.abs(p - math.round(p)) < 1e-9 ? str.tostring(int(math.round(p))) :
      str.tostring(p, format.mintick)



// The tail of a panel row: the count's standing against the nearest kihon
// suchi number, and the colour that standing earns.
//
// "no data" and "too far" are different answers. The first means the history
// is not there to count; the second means the count was refused because the
// anchor is further back than KIHON_SPAN_CAP periods, where the exact figure
// would cost a large history load to say something "past 257" already says.
rowTail(c, tooFar) =>
    tail = ""
    col = InpPanelColor
    if tooFar
        tail := "too far"                      // refused, and it will stay refused
    else if c <= 0
        tail := "no data"
    else
        off = kihonOffset(c, InpKihonCompound)
        mag = math.abs(off)
        if off == 0
            // "KS" rather than the whole word. It is the only thing in the row
            // that repeats, and shouting it in a column of counts made the
            // numbers - which are the reading - the quieter half.
            tail := "KS"
            col := InpPanelHit
        else if mag <= InpPanelNearTol
            // The sign reads the way the chart does: "-2" is two candles short
            // of a number, "+2" two candles past one.
            tail := "KS " + (off > 0 ? "+" : "-") + str.tostring(mag)
            col := InpPanelNear
        else
            // Past the last number there is nothing left to count to, so say
            // that rather than print a countdown to nowhere. The last number is
            // the last of the ACTIVE list: with the compounds switched off the
            // series ends at 26, not at 257.
            nx = kihonNext(c, InpKihonCompound)
            tail := nx == 0 ? "past " + str.tostring(kihonLast(InpKihonCompound)) :
                 str.tostring(nx) + " in " + str.tostring(nx - c)
    [tail, col]


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  Panel rows
//
//  Built into parallel arrays the way the MQL builds its string and colour
//  arrays, then written into one table at the end. Pine passes arrays by
//  reference, so these push straight into the caller's buffers.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

KP_MAX_ROWS = 24

// One row onto the end, or nothing if the panel is already full.
pushRow(mk, tf, ct, tl, cl, m, t, c, l, col) =>
    if array.size(mk) < KP_MAX_ROWS
        array.push(mk, m)
        array.push(tf, t)
        array.push(ct, c)
        array.push(tl, l)
        array.push(cl, col)

// A spacer. It reserves a row and draws nothing, which is the gap between
// blocks.
pushGap(mk, tf, ct, tl, cl) =>
    pushRow(mk, tf, ct, tl, cl, "", "", "", "", InpPanelColor)

// A block title: what, then the open everything under it counts from.
pushTitle(mk, tf, ct, tl, cl, title, anchorMs, dateOnly, col) =>
    when = na(anchorMs) ? "-" :
         str.format_time(anchorMs, dateOnly ? "yyyy.MM.dd" : "HH:mm", syminfo.timezone)
    pushRow(mk, tf, ct, tl, cl, "", title, "", "from " + when, col)

// One counted row: the marker for the chart's own timeframe, the name, the
// count, and what it owes the next number. The marker is decided by period
// LENGTH rather than by name, so a broker's non-standard period still marks
// itself correctly.
pushCount(mk, tf, ct, tl, cl, name, secs, c, anchorMs) =>
    far = secs > 0 and not na(anchorMs) and
         (timenow - anchorMs) / 1000 / secs > KIHON_SPAN_CAP
    [tail, col] = rowTail(c, far)
    pushRow(mk, tf, ct, tl, cl, secs == chartSecs ? ">" : "", name,
         c > 0 ? str.tostring(c) : "-", tail, col)


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  Drawing
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

var gLines  = array.new_line()
var gLabels = array.new_label()

var mkA  = array.new_string()
var tfA  = array.new_string()
var ctA  = array.new_string()
var tlA  = array.new_string()
var clA  = array.new_color()
var smkA = array.new_string()
var stfA = array.new_string()
var sctA = array.new_string()
var stlA = array.new_string()
var sclA = array.new_color()

// Both blocks live in one table: same top edge, one spacer column between
// them. Pine pins a table to one of nine positions rather than to a pixel
// offset, so Corner and "Centre it vertically" survive the port and the X and
// Y distances do not.
panelPos = InpPanelCorner == "Left upper" ?
         (InpPanelMiddle ? position.middle_left : position.top_left) :
     InpPanelCorner == "Left lower" ?
         (InpPanelMiddle ? position.middle_left : position.bottom_left) :
     InpPanelCorner == "Right upper" ?
         (InpPanelMiddle ? position.middle_right : position.top_right) :
         (InpPanelMiddle ? position.middle_right : position.bottom_right)

sessionPos = InpSessionPos == "Top left" ? position.top_left :
     InpSessionPos == "Top right" ? position.top_right :
     InpSessionPos == "Bottom left" ? position.bottom_left : position.bottom_right

// Created once and rewritten in place rather than swept and rebuilt, which is
// the MQL's approach too: there is no window in which the panel is missing,
// and a steady panel does not flicker.
var panel = table.new(panelPos, 9, KP_MAX_ROWS,
     bgcolor = InpPanelBox ? InpPanelBg : color.new(color.black, 100),
     border_color = InpPanelBox ? InpPanelBorder : color.new(color.black, 100),
     border_width = 1, frame_color = InpPanelBorder,
     frame_width = InpPanelBox ? 1 : 0)

var sessionBox = table.new(sessionPos, 1, 1, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 100))

// The session clock's zero. Pine has no terminal global to keep it across a
// reload, so this is the moment the script started running on this chart -
// which, unlike the MetaTrader build, a timeframe change resets.
var sessionStart   = timenow
var sessionAlerted = false

if barstate.islast
    // ── Sweep ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    while array.size(gLines) > 0
        line.delete(array.pop(gLines))
    while array.size(gLabels) > 0
        label.delete(array.pop(gLabels))

    array.clear(mkA)
    array.clear(tfA)
    array.clear(ctA)
    array.clear(tlA)
    array.clear(clA)
    array.clear(smkA)
    array.clear(stfA)
    array.clear(sctA)
    array.clear(stlA)
    array.clear(sclA)
    table.clear(panel, 0, 0, 8, KP_MAX_ROWS - 1)

    // Pine's 500-object ceilings, split between the things that want them. The
    // kihon marks are few and always drawn; the level lines and labels take
    // what is left, and the panel reports any label the budget refused rather
    // than dropping it quietly.
    labelBudget = 500 - (InpNumberAll ? 300 : 0) - 20
    labelsDropped = 0
    tick = syminfo.mintick

    // ── Levels ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // Collect every ticked grid's window around price, merge levels that land
    // on the same price under the highest PO3 number, draw.
    //
    // Powers of three nest: 27 is a multiple of 9, so every 27 level sits
    // exactly on a 9 level. Drawing both would stack two objects on one price
    // with the colour decided by whichever drew last. Instead a level is drawn
    // ONCE and belongs to the HIGHEST ticked PO3 number that lands on it.
    // Grids are walked ascending, so a later grid always outranks an earlier
    // one and ownership comes out order-independent.
    po3s = array.from(3, 9, 27, 81, 243, 729, 2187, 6561, 19683)
    ons  = array.from(InpUse_3, InpUse_9, InpUse_27, InpUse_81, InpUse_243,
         InpUse_729, InpUse_2187, InpUse_6561, InpUse_19683)
    cols = array.from(InpCol_3, InpCol_9, InpCol_27, InpCol_81, InpCol_243,
         InpCol_729, InpCol_2187, InpCol_6561, InpCol_19683)

    raws  = array.new_int()
    owner = array.new_int()

    for s = 0 to array.size(po3s) - 1
        if array.get(ons, s)
            po3 = array.get(po3s, s)
            m0  = po3Index(close, po3, InpScale)
            for m = m0 - InpEachSide + 1 to m0 + InpEachSide
                if m > 0                       // zero anchor and negatives are not prices
                    raw = m * po3
                    idx = array.indexof(raws, raw)
                    if idx == -1
                        if array.size(raws) < 480
                            array.push(raws, raw)
                            array.push(owner, s)
                    else
                        array.set(owner, idx, s)   // stronger number owns the level

    if array.size(raws) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(raws) - 1
            raw = array.get(raws, i)
            s   = array.get(owner, i)
            po3 = array.get(po3s, s)
            col = array.get(cols, s)
            px  = raw / InpScale

            // Width and style follow magnitude, so the bigger numbers read as
            // the stronger levels: 3/9/27 thin dotted, 81/243 thin solid,
            // 729/2187 medium, 6561/19683 thick.
            w   = po3 >= 6561 ? 3 : po3 >= 729 ? 2 : 1
            sty = po3 <= 27 ? line.style_dotted : line.style_solid

            array.push(gLines, line.new(bar_index - 1, px, bar_index, px,
                 xloc = xloc.bar_index, extend = extend.both,
                 color = col, style = sty, width = w))

            // Every label shares one time anchor, so the fine grids can pile
            // digits on top of each other: 3 puts levels $3 apart, far closer
            // than a line of text is tall. The threshold thins them - raise it
            // to label the stronger grids only.
            if InpShowLabels and po3 >= InpLabelMinPO3
                if array.size(gLabels) < labelBudget
                    // The label carries the OWNING PO3 number, so a merged
                    // level reads as the strongest grid that produced it,
                    // matching the colour it was given.
                    //
                    // Past the last candle the text reads RIGHTWARDS from the
                    // anchor, so the gap is the space between the candles and
                    // the number and the column lines up on its left edge, out
                    // in the margin beside the price scale. At or behind the
                    // last candle it ends at the anchor instead, which is what
                    // keeps it on screen with no right margin to read into -
                    // the same rule the countdown follows.
                    array.push(gLabels, label.new(bar_index + InpLabelShift, px,
                         str.tostring(po3), xloc = xloc.bar_index,
                         style = InpLabelShift > 0 ? label.style_label_left :
                              label.style_label_right,
                         color = color.new(color.black, 100), textcolor = col,
                         size = InpFontSize,
                         tooltip = priceText(px) + "   " + str.tostring(po3) +
                              " x " + str.tostring(int(raw / po3))))
                else
                    labelsDropped := labelsDropped + 1

    // ── The count marked on the chart ────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // Anchored to each candle's own time and to that candle's low, so the
    // numbers sit clear of the body rather than across it.
    if InpShowCount and cChart > 0
        aShift = cChart - 1                    // candle 1 lives this far back

        if InpMarkOpen and aShift >= 0 and aShift < 2000 and aShift <= bar_index
            b = bar_index - aShift
            array.push(gLines, line.new(b, low[aShift], b, high[aShift],
                 xloc = xloc.bar_index, extend = extend.both,
                 color = InpOpenColor, style = line.style_dotted, width = 1))
            array.push(gLabels, label.new(b, low[aShift] - InpKihonGapPts * tick,
                 "1", xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_up,
                 color = color.new(color.black, 100), textcolor = InpOpenColor,
                 size = InpKihonSize))

        if InpMarkKihon
            lastK = InpKihonCompound ? KIHON_COUNT : KIHON_SIMPLE
            for i = 0 to lastK - 1
                k = array.get(KIHON, i)
                if k > cChart                  // not reached yet
                    break
                back = aShift - (k - 1)
                if back >= 0 and back < 2000 and back <= bar_index
                    kcol = i < KIHON_SIMPLE ? InpKihonSimple : InpKihonComp
                    b = bar_index - back
                    if InpKihonLines
                        // Dotted and dimmed: a time marker that hides the
                        // candle it marks has defeated itself, and Pine cannot
                        // put a line behind the candles the way MT5 can.
                        array.push(gLines, line.new(b, low[back], b, high[back],
                             xloc = xloc.bar_index, extend = extend.both,
                             color = color.new(kcol, 65),
                             style = line.style_dotted, width = 1))
                    array.push(gLabels, label.new(b,
                         low[back] - InpKihonGapPts * tick, str.tostring(k),
                         xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_up,
                         color = color.new(color.black, 100), textcolor = kcol,
                         size = InpKihonSize,
                         tooltip = "candle " + str.tostring(k)))

        // Plain numbers on the rest. Drawn after the kihon marks and skipping
        // them, so a kihon candle keeps its own colour instead of being
        // overwritten by a neutral label of the same number. A whole day of M1
        // is 1440 labels, so only the most recent run is numbered.
        if InpNumberAll
            firstN = cChart > 300 ? cChart - 300 + 1 : 1
            for k = firstN to cChart
                skip = (k == 1 and InpMarkOpen) or
                     (InpMarkKihon and kihonIs(k, InpKihonCompound))
                back = aShift - (k - 1)
                if not skip and back >= 0 and back < 2000 and
                     back <= bar_index and array.size(gLabels) < 495
                    array.push(gLabels, label.new(bar_index - back,
                         low[back] - InpKihonGapPts * tick, str.tostring(k),
                         xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_up,
                         color = color.new(color.black, 100),
                         textcolor = InpPanelColor, size = size.tiny))

    // ── The countdown on the developing candle ───────────────────────────────
    //
    // Anchored to the last bar and to the current price, so the text travels
    // with the candle as the chart scrolls and rides price as it moves. Past
    // the last bar it reads rightwards into the empty space; at or behind it
    // the text ends at the anchor, which keeps it on screen.
    if InpShowClock
        left = int((time_close - timenow) / 1000)
        array.push(gLabels, label.new(bar_index + InpClockShift,
             close + InpClockGapPts * tick, chartTf + "  " + hms(left),
             xloc = xloc.bar_index,
             style = InpClockShift > 0 ? label.style_label_left :
                  label.style_label_right,
             color = color.new(color.black, 100), textcolor = InpClockColor,
             size = InpClockSize))

    // ── The count panel ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // A ladder of calendar periods, each counted in the candles that divide it.
    // Every block carries its OWN anchor, which is the whole point - a week
    // count from the day open would read 1 forever.
    //
    // M30 sits on the week because that is where it fits: a trading week is 240
    // M30 candles, so the count runs through eleven of the twelve numbers and
    // stops just short of 257 without ever running off the end of the list.
    if InpShowPanel
        if InpShowYear
            pushTitle(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA, "Year", yearOpen, true, InpPanelColor)
            pushCount(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA, "MN1", SEC_MN1, cMN1_Y, yearOpen)
            pushCount(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA, "W1",  SEC_W1,  cW1_Y,  yearOpen)
            pushCount(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA, "D1",  SEC_D1,  cD1_Y,  yearOpen)

        if InpShowMonth
            if array.size(mkA) > 0
                pushGap(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA)
            pushTitle(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA, "Month", monthOpen, true, InpPanelColor)
            pushCount(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA, "D1", SEC_D1, cD1_M, monthOpen)
            pushCount(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA, "H4", SEC_H4, cH4_M, monthOpen)
            pushCount(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA, "H1", SEC_H1, cH1_M, monthOpen)

        if InpShowWeek
            if array.size(mkA) > 0
                pushGap(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA)
            pushTitle(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA, "Week", weekOpen, true, InpPanelColor)
            pushCount(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA, "H4",  SEC_H4,  cH4_W,  weekOpen)
            pushCount(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA, "H1",  SEC_H1,  cH1_W,  weekOpen)
            pushCount(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA, "M30", SEC_M30, cM30_W, weekOpen)

        if InpShowDay
            if array.size(mkA) > 0
                pushGap(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA)
            // Titled "Sess" when the chart's anchor is a custom session time,
            // so the panel says which open it is counting from.
            pushTitle(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA, daySess ? "Sess" : "Day", dayOpen,
                 false, InpPanelColor)

            // H1 down to the CHART's own period and no finer: detail finer than
            // the candles in front of you is a count of something you cannot
            // see. H1 is always kept, so an H4 or daily chart still gets the
            // hour count rather than an empty block.
            pushCount(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA, "H1", SEC_H1, cH1_D, dayOpen)
            if SEC_M30 >= chartSecs
                pushCount(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA, "M30", SEC_M30, cM30_D, dayOpen)
            if SEC_M15 >= chartSecs
                pushCount(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA, "M15", SEC_M15, cM15_D, dayOpen)
            if SEC_M5 >= chartSecs
                pushCount(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA, "M5", SEC_M5, cM5_D, dayOpen)

            // The nested M1 row, on every period - it is the one row carrying
            // information none of the others do. The label carries the hour it
            // restarted at, because the count alone cannot tell you which phase
            // of the day it is measuring.
            pushCount(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA,
                 "M1@" + (segNo > 0 ? str.tostring(segNo) : "-"),
                 SEC_M1, cM1_N, dayOpen)

    // Pine's own limit, said out loud. It only appears when the budget actually
    // refused a label, so a chart inside the budget never carries the row.
    if labelsDropped > 0
        if array.size(mkA) > 0
            pushGap(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA)
        pushRow(mkA, tfA, ctA, tlA, clA, "", "labels", str.tostring(labelsDropped),
             "over budget", InpPanelNear)

    // ── The segment block ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // When an H4 or an H1 count stands ON a number, the candle carrying that
    // number IS a kihon candle, and it is one for its whole length. The panel
    // beside it says that hour is due a turn; it cannot say where in the hour
    // you are. So this block counts the candles INSIDE that candle, from its
    // open.
    //
    // An H4 is checked against the month and week anchors, an H1 against the
    // month, week and day. H4 gets no day anchor because a trading day holds
    // six H4 candles, so a day-anchored H4 count stops at 6 and could never
    // reach 9. These are read from the counts directly, so the block says the
    // same thing whether or not the row that would show the hit is switched on.
    //
    // The section reads "none" most of the time and keeps its title rather than
    // vanishing, so the space stays accounted for.
    if InpShowSeg
        pushRow(smkA, stfA, sctA, stlA, sclA, "", "Kihon Suchi segments", "", "",
             InpPanelColor)

        h4Hit = InpSegH4 and
             ((cH4_M > 0 and kihonIs(cH4_M, InpKihonCompound)) or
              (cH4_W > 0 and kihonIs(cH4_W, InpKihonCompound)))
        h1Hit = InpSegH1 and
             ((cH1_M > 0 and kihonIs(cH1_M, InpKihonCompound)) or
              (cH1_W > 0 and kihonIs(cH1_W, InpKihonCompound)) or
              (cH1_D > 0 and kihonIs(cH1_D, InpKihonCompound)))

        // Everything in the block counts from the candle, and nothing from a
        // calendar. The header reads "H4 from 08:00" and every row under it is
        // measured from that open. It is in the hit colour because the candle
        // it names IS the hit; the rows below colour themselves on their own
        // counts, against the same numbers and the same tolerance as every
        // other row.
        //
        // Which rows appear is decided by what fits - a row is shown only when
        // at least one kihon number can be reached inside the candle. Sixteen
        // M15 candles fit in an H4, so 9 is in reach; the four that fit in an
        // H1 could never read anything but a countdown, which is why M15 is in
        // the H4 box and not the H1 box. Same rule that keeps the day anchor
        // off the H4 count, applied at the other end of the nesting.
        first = array.get(KIHON, 0)

        if h4Hit
            pushTitle(smkA, stfA, sctA, stlA, sclA, "H4", h4Open, false, InpPanelHit)
            if SEC_H4 / SEC_M15 >= first
                pushCount(smkA, stfA, sctA, stlA, sclA, "M15", SEC_M15, sM15_H4, h4Open)
            if SEC_H4 / SEC_M5 >= first
                pushCount(smkA, stfA, sctA, stlA, sclA, "M5", SEC_M5, sM5_H4, h4Open)
            if SEC_H4 / SEC_M1 >= first
                pushCount(smkA, stfA, sctA, stlA, sclA, "M1", SEC_M1, sM1_H4, h4Open)

        if h1Hit
            // The gap goes in only when an H4 block came first, so a lone H1
            // block is not pushed away from the title by an empty row.
            if h4Hit
                pushGap(smkA, stfA, sctA, stlA, sclA)
            pushTitle(smkA, stfA, sctA, stlA, sclA, "H1", h1Open, false, InpPanelHit)
            // No M15 row here, and this is where the rule bites: SEC_H1 /
            // SEC_M15 is 4, short of the first number, so an M15 count inside
            // an hour could never read anything but a countdown. It is not
            // requested at all rather than requested and hidden.
            if SEC_H1 / SEC_M5 >= first
                pushCount(smkA, stfA, sctA, stlA, sclA, "M5", SEC_M5, sM5_H1, h1Open)
            if SEC_H1 / SEC_M1 >= first
                pushCount(smkA, stfA, sctA, stlA, sclA, "M1", SEC_M1, sM1_H1, h1Open)

        if not h4Hit and not h1Hit
            pushRow(smkA, stfA, sctA, stlA, sclA, "", "none", "", "", InpPanelColor)

    // ── Both blocks into the one table ───────────────────────────────────────
    nMain = array.size(mkA)
    nSeg  = array.size(smkA)
    rows  = math.max(nMain, nSeg)

    if rows > 0
        for r = 0 to rows - 1
            if r < nMain
                c = array.get(clA, r)
                table.cell(panel, 0, r, array.get(mkA, r), text_color = c,
                     text_size = InpPanelSize, text_halign = text.align_left)
                table.cell(panel, 1, r, array.get(tfA, r), text_color = c,
                     text_size = InpPanelSize, text_halign = text.align_left)
                table.cell(panel, 2, r, array.get(ctA, r), text_color = c,
                     text_size = InpPanelSize, text_halign = text.align_right)
                table.cell(panel, 3, r, array.get(tlA, r), text_color = c,
                     text_size = InpPanelSize, text_halign = text.align_left)
            if nSeg > 0
                // The gap between the two blocks. Pine sizes a table column to
                // its widest cell, so a column of spaces is the pixel gap.
                table.cell(panel, 4, r, "   ", text_size = InpPanelSize)
            if r < nSeg
                c = array.get(sclA, r)
                table.cell(panel, 5, r, array.get(smkA, r), text_color = c,
                     text_size = InpPanelSize, text_halign = text.align_left)
                table.cell(panel, 6, r, array.get(stfA, r), text_color = c,
                     text_size = InpPanelSize, text_halign = text.align_left)
                table.cell(panel, 7, r, array.get(sctA, r), text_color = c,
                     text_size = InpPanelSize, text_halign = text.align_right)
                table.cell(panel, 8, r, array.get(stlA, r), text_color = c,
                     text_size = InpPanelSize, text_halign = text.align_left)

    // ── The session timer ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // Wall-clock time this chart has been open. It counts through closed
    // markets and weekends, since the point is screen time, not session time,
    // and turns red once a set number of minutes is up.
    if InpShowSession
        elapsed = int((timenow - sessionStart) / 1000)
        over = InpSessionLimit > 0 and elapsed >= InpSessionLimit * 60
        table.cell(sessionBox, 0, 0, "On chart  " + hms(elapsed),
             text_color = over ? InpSessionOver : InpSessionColor,
             text_size = InpSessionSize)
    else
        table.clear(sessionBox, 0, 0)

// One alert the moment the screen-time budget is spent, guarded so it fires
// once for the life of the script.
if InpShowSession and InpSessionLimit > 0 and not sessionAlerted and
     (timenow - sessionStart) / 1000 >= InpSessionLimit * 60
    sessionAlerted := true
    alert(syminfo.ticker + ": " + str.tostring(InpSessionLimit) +
         " minutes on the chart.", alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// A candle standing on a kihon number on the chart's own timeframe.
//
// A caution: the count is arithmetic, not a signal. It says where a turn is
// DUE, never that one is happening and never which way. Nothing here acts on
// these numbers.
kihonNow = InpShowCount and cChart > 0 and kihonIs(cChart, InpKihonCompound)
alertcondition(kihonNow, "Kihon suchi candle",
     "Candle count has reached a kihon suchi number")
